+# Report of the hand H-Bell-Through-The-Cone-2 (bc2): Bell read through the root by the law's own run back (2026-10-26, 02:47 to 02:5x UTC)
+
+**Verdict line: DOES NOT. The bound stays at 2 through the root. The reason by name: the root's integers are a function of the birth and are the same under the four settings; the backward run is a bijection that writes nothing at the root and carries no setting (a setting is the decoder's pair of integers, never an integer of the Node nor a line of the books); the outcomes stay functions of their own Nodes, read for all four settings at once on every click, so the per-pair identity is -2 or 2 at every pair and |S| <= 2 by every reading, at the clicks and through the root; S^2 > 8 is not read. Measured on four worlds at this head: the hole 60 (16 pairs), the chiral 60 and 300 (17 pairs), qg1's AB edge world (16 pairs); the run back exact at every interval, 60 of 60, 60 of 60, 300 of 300, 30 of 30.**
+
+Worktree detached at 910648f74 (the merge of toys-5 2ab32b518). Files under tools/derivations/open_items/H-Bell-Through-The-Cone-2/ (root_read.py the reader, test_bc2.py the one test, world_chiral_300.json and world_two_slits_AB.json the two world files with the universe path resolved from this folder, out/*.json and out/*.txt the readings, bc2.patch the patch). Python /home/user/Universe24/venv314/bin/python, PYTHONPATH=<worktree>/src, TMPDIR=/dev/shm/tmp, nice -n 19. No act of the engine or of the decoder touched; no edit under src/ or tests/; no commit. Integers only, ASCII. No non-local form proposed, built or measured; the one non-local form the question touches is named and refused in section 5.
+
+## 1. The owner's reading, as read by this hand
+
+"Bell's bound stands without a violation of nature, because of the cone and the time reversal." Read as: the two children part at one Link and click at two Nodes; each click is a function of its own Node (QG-S3, the bound 2); but the law's record runs backward exactly (the run back, every act its own inverse), so from each click the time reversal within the cone reaches the birth's Link, where the two children were one meeting; a correlation computed through that root is local in the law's sense (every step one Link, forward or backward) and not a function of one Node's state at one time. The question put: does that reading give S^2 > 8, or does the root add nothing.
+
+## 2. The derivation from the letter
+
+### 2.1 What the record carries at the birth's Link that both children share (the root)
+
+The birth line (close.births; the record's `birth` event) carries, for the one meeting of the two ends: the children's record `line_pair` (0, 1 or 2 on the toy's three planes); the senses [-1, 1]; `W_children` [-(T div 2), +(T div 2)] = [-18000, 18000] at the toy's T (13 of 17 on the chiral at exactly -+18000, 4 with a child's W above by its standing; 16 of 16 on the hole and the AB world); the lay's levels `amplitude` [a, b] = [125, 144] on every birth of every world read (66 of 66), laid (a, 0, 0, -b) at `minus` and (a, 0, 0, +b) at `plus`: the same re level, the im levels opposite, the conjugate pair at the Link's two ends; the taken row and line, the taker's levels at the take (`taken_now_was`, `taker`), the room, the proper count and the content. The Node's remainders at the lay are not on the birth line; they are in the state at the birth's interval, which the run back recovers (2.2). Everything in the root is written at the birth's interval i_b from the state within i_b Links of the birth (the cone's run is the board's run, L306): a function of the seed and of nothing read later.
+
+### 2.2 The backward run from a click to its birth within the cone
+
+The run back is the whole board's step at -1 (node.step_back = run(-1); run.run_back): the same acts in the reverse order, Rule3 inverted by the kept remainder (a bijection), the held writes by theirs, the swap its own involution, and the close undone from the books (close.unclick: every birth's two lays removed from the birth line's `amplitude`, every take's line restored from `taken_now_was`, the readings' counters restored; the click's inverse is "crossed from the board's lines beside the click line, by the remainder and the count", ALGEBRA.md's table). Backward the reach is one Link per interval as forward: a Node's state at i - 1 is a function of its own and its six neighbours' at i. So the cone of a click at the Node n at the interval i_c reaches the birth's Link at i_b when the Link distance from n to the Link is at most d = i_c - i_b.
+
+Measured (root_read.py: the state's hash kept at every interval forward, the board run back from the last interval to the first, each interval compared bit for bit): the run back exact 60 of 60 (hole 60), 60 of 60 (chiral 60), 300 of 300 (chiral 300), 30 of 30 (AB); every pair's intervals from the birth to the clicks exact. The intervals back per pair: hole 60 (1, 10), (10, 1) at the 8 births of the interval 9, (4, 2) at the 4 of 19, (3, 6) at the 4 of 20, the longest 10; chiral (5, 9) ... (3, 12), the longest 12; AB (3, 1) ... (1, 14), the longest 14. The Link distance from every click's Node to the birth's Link: 0 at 49 of 49 pairs on every world (the child clicks at the Node where it was laid; the ends one Link apart, QG-M6 standing). So every click's cone holds its birth with d - 0 intervals to spare, and the integers that reach the root are every integer of the state at the birth's interval: the run back is bit for bit, by the hash of every level and every remainder (node.state_bytes).
+
+What the backward run carries from a click, by name: the click's realised outcome, yes: the credit line is in the books and the frame's levels (re_now, im_now at the click) are restored into the state as the run passes the click. The click's realised setting, no: a setting is the decoder's pair (p, q) read against the frame, sign(p re_now + q im_now); it is not an integer of the Node, not a line of the books, and no act forward or backward reads or writes it. On the record every click carries, at once, its outcome under every setting (the four here; any pair the frame or the sense can be read by).
+
+### 2.3 The reading through the root
+
+Per pair: the root R recovered from the minus click's backward run and from the plus click's is the same R (one state at one interval; the hash equal). The outcome at the minus end at the setting a is A(a) = sign(p re_now + q im_now) at its click; the state at its click is the forward run of d_minus intervals from the root along its own track, deterministic, one Link per interval; so A(a) = f(a, R, the track of the minus child), and likewise B(b) = g(b, R, the track of the plus child). The track of the minus child does not contain b, and R does not: R is written at i_b and read bit for bit; "root integers equal under the four settings" is true by the letter, not by chance, since no setting enters the board. This is Bell's local deterministic form with lambda = R and the two tracks, and the record carries the four outcomes of every click side by side, so per pair the identity
+
+A(a) B(b) - A(a) B(b') + A(a') B(b) + A(a') B(b') = A(a) [B(b) - B(b')] + A(a') [B(b) + B(b')]
+
+is -2 or 2 (0 where a frame's axis reads exactly 0), and S over the pairs is the mean of the identities: |S| <= 2 by every reading, through the root or not. Measured, S at the clicks by the frame's axis with the identity per pair: hole 60 S = -16 / 16 = -1 exactly, {-2: 12, 2: 4}, E = [12, 4, -16, -8] / 16; chiral 60 and 300 S = -6 / 17 (-36 hundredths), {-2: 10, 2: 7}, E = [5, 9, -1, -1] / 17; AB S = -8 / 16 (-50 hundredths), {-2: 10, 2: 6}, E = [0, 0, -4, -4] / 16. By the sense: E = -1 at every setting pair and S = -2 exactly, 16 of 16, 17 of 17, 17 of 17, 16 of 16 (the children's senses opposite at the birth and at the click on every pair, including the AB world where qg1's older head read 8 of 26 mixed; at this head the generic close pairs every click with its own birth). Through the root itself, the root's integers read as the outcome: by the frame's axis the lay's levels (125, 0) at both ends give sign(125 p) = +1 at every setting, E = +1, S = 32 / 16 = 2 and 34 / 17 = 2, the identity {2: all}; by the senses at the root S = -2 exactly. S^2 > 8 is read false by every one of the four readings on every world (the integer test num^2 against 8 den^2: 256 against 2048, 36 against 2312, 64 against 2048 by the frame at the clicks).
+
+Why the root adds nothing, in one line each: (i) R is a function of the birth's interval state, the seed within i_b Links, written before any click and the same under every setting; (ii) the backward run restores and writes nothing (every act its own inverse), so there is no realised port written at the birth; 4.0's clause of that name was a write at the root, an act, and non-local; (iii) the setting is the decoder's and never on the board, so neither the forward nor the backward run carries it to the root or past it; (iv) hence A(a) is independent of b, the outcomes stay functions of their own Nodes, and the counterfactual table on every click gives the identity -2 or 2 per pair. S^2 > 8 needs A(a) to differ by whether b or b' is read at the other end, which is a read that is not a function of one Node (QG-S3's clause), the thing the owner's law refuses and this hand does not propose.
+
+### 2.4 The owner's sentence against the finding
+
+The cone and the time reversal are real in the law and measured here: the root is reached from every click, bit for bit. They make the root a common cause, and a common cause is exactly what Bell's bound is a theorem about. So the bound 2 stands in the law through the root as at the clicks, and it stands against nature's S^2 > 8 (row 56 a finding against nature, beside parity's and spin's, as QG-S3 holds). The owner's reading that the bound stands is derived; that it stands "without a violation of nature" is not: the law's 2 against nature's 2 sqrt 2 is the violation, and the cone and the time reversal do not close it.
+
+## 3. The sentence BC-S1 for ALGEBRA.md (under The click is the meeting, after QG-S3; dated 2026-10-26, the hand bc2; the owner's word owed)
+
+**BC-S1, Bell through the root.** The run back from a click reaches its birth's Link within the cone (one Link per interval backward as forward) and recovers every integer of the state at the birth bit for bit, the same root from both ends; the root is a function of the birth and of no setting, since a setting is a read of the frame and no act writes it, and the run back writes nothing; so a correlation read through the root is Bell's local form with the root as the common cause, the per-pair identity A(a) B(b) - A(a) B(b') + A(a') B(b) + A(a') B(b') is -2 or 2 at every pair, and |S| <= 2 through the root as at the clicks; S^2 > 8 is read SHOWN by no reading that is a function of each end's own Node, forward or backward (row 56 stands as QG-S3 holds it).
